From 6e0450db30829641e65775dd6181f2720572c418 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: olympia <olympia@xbmc.org>
Date: Thu, 29 Oct 2026 12:50:24 +0100
Subject: [PATCH] [BackgroundInfoLoader] Allow an item to be held back from the
 loader

The loader thread sets art, properties and other details on the items
of a list without a lock, so another thread could only read or change an
item safely after stopping the loader. Stopping waits for the item the
loader is working on, however long its lookup takes. An item can now be
held instead, and the hold only waits while the loader thread is working
on that very item. The loader thread puts a held item aside, goes on with
the other items, and loads the held item between them once it is
released, at the latest after them, still the cached stuff before the
lookup.

The observer is now called before the loader thread lets go of the item,
as it may change the item as well.

The tests cover that a held item is loaded once it is released, that a
hold waits only for the item the loader is working on, and that stopping
the loader wakes it while it waits for a held item.
